cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Numen Pathfinding Benchmark: GRAV3D, a 3D grid pathfinding benchmark with gravity, climbing, swimming and block editing"
type: dataset
version: v3
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dwinovo/numen-pathfinding-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/Dwinovo/numen-pathfinding-benchmark"
authors:
  - name: "Dwinovo"
abstract: >-
  Seven fixed 512x512 terrain regions generated by Minecraft 1.21.1 (overworld biomes, caves, nether),
  exported as a plain byte grid with a documented class table, 840 problems in three distance buckets,
  and optimal reference answers and paths under the GRAV3D rules (track A: no editing; track E: dig, bridge,
  pillar). Includes a validator and a reference solver (MIT) so that results can be checked without Minecraft.
keywords:
  - pathfinding
  - benchmark
  - 3D grid
  - Minecraft
  - A*
